(5332567, 769165, 47483, '<td valign="top">"I wanted a unique title, so at first, I was going to choose the name of a star in the constellation Draco... but didnt see anything I liked. I eventually was able to find Nagendra in a search, and learned that Nagendra was sanskrit for "Lord of Snakes", and I thought it was perfect."<br/> <br/>Yaa very apt name from indian context. <br/> <br/>This word nagendra is made up of nag (snake) + indra (master of gods plus many things). <br/> <br/>But god shiva is called god of snakes (if i am right).<br/> <br/></td>', '"I wanted a unique title, so at first, I was going to choose the name of a star in the constellation Draco... but didnt see anything I liked. I eventually was able to find Nagendra in a search, and learned that Nagendra was sanskrit for "Lord of Snakes", and I thought it was perfect." Yaa very apt name from indian context.  This word nagendra is made up of nag (snake) + indra (master of gods plus many things).  But god shiva is called god of snakes (if i am right). ', '2009-03-13 06:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
